# Copy to apps/web/.env if you want the dev server to proxy the API.
#
# Relative: requests go to the Vite dev server, which proxies /api to the Nest
# server on port 5001 (see vite.config.ts). Same-origin, so no CORS.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# Absolute also works — src/api.ts falls back to this when the var is unset,
# and bootstrap.ts enables CORS for FRONTEND_URL plus CORS_ORIGINS:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5001/api

# Deployed, nothing sets this by hand: scripts/deploy-web.sh reads the stack's
# ApiEndpoint output and builds against the absolute API Gateway URL, so the
# deployed SPA calls the API cross-origin.
#
# The relative form does NOT work deployed. Worth stating, because it fails
# quietly rather than loudly: the CloudFront distribution has one origin — the
# S3 bucket — and no /api behaviour, so a request to /api/... reaches S3, 404s,
# and the SPA fallback turns that into index.html with a 200. The client gets
# HTML where it expects JSON, with no connection error to point at the cause.
# infra/template.yaml says the same thing where it sets CORS_ORIGINS: "every
# deployed API call is cross-origin".
